Drop the Ripgrep WORKSPACE stanzas the public mirror cannot satisfy

WORKSPACE.linux loads //Vendors/Ripgrep:repositories.bzl, but Vendors/Ripgrep is
absent from SYNCLIST, so the public mirror never receives the directory. A
WORKSPACE load() is eager, so every commit from 3dc01fe5 onward fails at load
phase for anyone building the community repo. Nothing outside the two WORKSPACE
files names ripgrep, so removing the load, the ripgrep_repositories() call and
the @ripgrep_crates load costs the Linux build no target.

It does cost one transitive pin. ripgrep_repositories() reaches
rules_rust_dependencies(), which is what declared rules_license 1.0.0 first and
so kept the stale 0.0.3 that the apple and swift rule sets carry from winning.
protobuf 32.0 calls license() without license_kinds, mandatory in 0.0.3 alone,
which fails analysis for every //Apps target. Pinning rules_license beside the
protobuf and rules_cc pins restores it, in the same idiom and for the same
reason.
